From 2c9dd9c909a26478cc398c0060cd3e6f41327840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Dymarek <gregd72002@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:08:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] lantiq: add support for DrayTek Vigor 2862

Hardware:
- SoC:      Lantiq xRX330 (GRX369, part 0x011, v1.1), MIPS 34Kc @ 600 MHz
            (2 VPEs)
- RAM:      128 MiB (top 1 MiB not used by Linux, holds the GPHY
            firmware copy)
- NAND:     128 MiB, Toshiba TC58NVG0S3E
- SPI-NOR:  256 KiB, MX25L2005 (DrayBoot bootloader and board data)
- Ethernet: 1x WAN (WAN2) on an AR8035 attached via RGMII,
            4x LAN on the SoC GPHYs
- DSL:      VDSL2/ADSL2+ (VRX318 on PCIe), not supported
- USB:      2x USB 2.0
- Buttons:  reset
- LEDs:     ACT, USB1, USB2, WAN2, DSL, QoS, WCF, VPN, DMZ, port LEDs
- Serial:   115200 8N1

Boot:
DrayBoot (SPI-NOR) loads 512 KiB from its NAND firmware slot at
0x1380000 and jumps to it. OpenWrt places a RAM-boot U-Boot there,
which boots the kernel from 0x1480000; the rootfs is UBI from
0x1880000 up to DrayBoot's backup slot at 0x3380000, so the stock
firmware kept there is preserved for recovery. The layout is the same
as on the Vigor 2860.

The GPHYs run from the firmware copy DrayBoot leaves in RAM; U-Boot
moves it to a reserved region and the switch driver boots the GPHYs
from it.

Front panel LAN1-LAN4 are switch ports 1, 4, 2 and 3; the port labels
and LEDs follow the panel.

Installation:
1. Enter the DrayBoot TFTP recovery
2. Set the computer to 192.168.1.2/24 and connect it to LAN1
3. Rename the factory image
   openwrt-lantiq-xrx200-draytek_vigor2862-squashfs-factory.bin to
   v2862x.bin. DrayBoot only accepts images whose name starts with the
   model; the character before .bin selects the action: '0' boots the
   image from memory, any other character writes it to NAND.
4. Upload the factory image:
   tftp -m binary 192.168.1.1 -c put v2862x.bin
5. DrayBoot writes the image to the primary firmware slot and boots
   OpenWrt; the backup slot keeps the stock firmware

Revert to stock:
DrayBoot verifies the primary slot checksum on every boot and restores
the backup slot (stock firmware) on a mismatch.

MAC addresses:
LAN   00:1d:aa:xx:xx:88  SPI-NOR 0x3fff8
WAN   +2

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Gregory Dymarek <gregd72002@gmail.com>
